Track 1: Locomotives Drink the Salt
- Story & Context: At the Choum junction, guitarist Amadou Cissé was bartering a sack of desert dates for a water-damaged Yamaha keyboard when a shunting diesel locomotive severed the depot's generator line with an ear-splitting pop. Amid the sharp reek of spilled fuel and scalding mint tea, the band hooked the keyboard straight into a dying truck battery, and the surviving frequency chip groaned back to life with a warped, microtonal lilt that matched the iron-ore train's sluggish Antillean clatter. Amadou plugged his foam-damped Stratocaster into the same line to soothe the shouting traders, falling into a cozy Afrobeat guitar groove that had the whole platform swaying in the dust. The reel-to-reel deck captured Amadou singing through his linen scarf right as the dust cleared: "Let the chassis rattle, love will carry the groove."
